      "tip_id": "STA-0003",
      "material": "stainless_steel",
      "category": "general",
      "tip_text": "Climb mill only — conventional milling rubs on exit and work-hardens the surface",
      "detail": "Conventional milling exits with zero chip thickness, causing rubbing. This creates a work-hardened surface for the next pass.",
      "sources": [
        {
